    "authorAssociation": "NONE",
    "body": "so imagine the completion option contains a new line (for example I'm overriding a method from the parent class in python, the completion consists of function signature, new line, and then super().methodname())\r\nbut the new line isn't inserted correctly and I have no Idea why! (also can't search google because it seems that google ignores the symbols in the search bar or gives them specific meanings!)\r\nany way!\r\ndesired behavior:\r\n1 - I accept the completion option\r\n2 - I get this\r\n\r\n```\r\nasync def find_peer(self, host: Node, identifier: UniversalPeerIdentifier) -> Peer:\r\n    return await super().find_peer(host, identifier)\r\n```\r\nactual behavior:\r\n1 - I accept the completion option\r\n2 - I get this\r\n\r\n```\r\nasync def find_peer(self, host: Node, identifier: UniversalPeerIdentifier) -> Peer:�    return await super().find_peer(host, identifier)\r\n```",
    "bodyHTML": "<p dir=\"auto\">so imagine the completion option contains a new line (for example I'm overriding a method from the parent class in python, the completion consists of function signature, new line, and then super().methodname())<br>\nbut the new line isn't inserted correctly and I have no Idea why! (also can't search google because it seems that google ignores the symbols in the search bar or gives them specific meanings!)<br>\nany way!<br>\ndesired behavior:<br>\n1 - I accept the completion option<br>\n2 - I get this</p>\n<div class=\"snippet-clipboard-content notranslate position-relative overflow-auto\" data-snippet-clipboard-copy-content=\"async def find_peer(self, host: Node, identifier: UniversalPeerIdentifier) -&gt; Peer:\n    return await super().find_peer(host, identifier)\"><pre class=\"notranslate\"><code class=\"notranslate\">async def find_peer(self, host: Node, identifier: UniversalPeerIdentifier) -&gt; Peer:\n    return await super().find_peer(host, identifier)\n</code></pre></div>\n<p dir=\"auto\">actual behavior:<br>\n1 - I accept the completion option<br>\n2 - I get this</p>\n<div class=\"snippet-clipboard-content notranslate position-relative overflow-auto\" data-snippet-clipboard-copy-content=\"async def find_peer(self, host: Node, identifier: UniversalPeerIdentifier) -&gt; Peer:�    return await super().find_peer(host, identifier)\"><pre class=\"notranslate\"><code class=\"notranslate\">async def find_peer(self, host: Node, identifier: UniversalPeerIdentifier) -&gt; Peer:�    return await super().find_peer(host, identifier)\n</code></pre></div>",
    "bodyText": "so imagine the completion option contains a new line (for example I'm overriding a method from the parent class in python, the completion consists of function signature, new line, and then super().methodname())\nbut the new line isn't inserted correctly and I have no Idea why! (also can't search google because it seems that google ignores the symbols in the search bar or gives them specific meanings!)\nany way!\ndesired behavior:\n1 - I accept the completion option\n2 - I get this\nasync def find_peer(self, host: Node, identifier: UniversalPeerIdentifier) -> Peer:\n    return await super().find_peer(host, identifier)\n\nactual behavior:\n1 - I accept the completion option\n2 - I get this\nasync def find_peer(self, host: Node, identifier: UniversalPeerIdentifier) -> Peer:�    return await super().find_peer(host, identifier)",
